module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.string_interpolates_a_name_that_is_not_a_value_in_scope

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BlockerClassUnstated, RecurringFailureMode, RungUnread }

data string_interpolates_a_name_that_is_not_a_value_in_scope: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "string_interpolates_a_name_that_is_not_a_value_in_scope" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a string literal holding a brace followed by an identifier (prose naming a Rust import list) is an interpolation hole, and the hole names something that is not a value in scope. Observed on gunbc#15495 at 7a81e3b: two receipt strings of a recurring_failure_mode row carried the text of a Rust import list with a braced type name, the closure typechecked, and the failure appeared only when the heal stage0 check evaluated the failure-mode roster: NoSuchVariable with the type's name, in an instrument unrelated to the row.",
    "HARM: a ledger row's prose broke an unrelated instrument, found by CI heal (non-required) after v2-bootstrap passed. EXECUTED: heal_stage0_overlap_refusal_wet exit 1 at 7a81e3b, exit 0 at its parent and with only the row removed (calm-crab-645, srv1); the escaped brace is the repair on the row (81ab4d6).",
    "RUNG NOT TYPED: whether the seed typecheck or the native compile refuses an interpolation of an undefined name has not been executed; the log shows typecheck completing on the closure, so the seed route accepted it. NEXT TRIGGER: execute a one-string fixture through the seed check and through the native compile; a refusal located at the hole is the ceiling (structurally guaranteed).",
    "RECOGNITION RULE: NoSuchVariable naming a type or a word that appears only inside a string literal; grep the string for a brace followed by an identifier."
    "RECURRENCE, 2026-11-02, PR #15636 at 5b0b26d9b399, IN A FAILURE-MODE ROW ABOUT ANOTHER SUBJECT: its receipt quoted the argv text of extdeps.rust.cargo_build, which really does contain a brace-hole (the injection writes CARGO_TARGET_DIR = the target-dir parameter), and quoting it verbatim made the row itself interpolate two names that are not in scope. EXECUTED: compiling that row module alone refused twice, undefined variable for each name -- 2 blocking, 0 advisory, exit 1 -- while the same tree compiled every importer cleanly, because NOTHING IMPORTS A DATA-ROW MODULE: the only routine reachability these rows have is CI heal and v2-bootstrap parsing the whole population, which is why the red arrived 16 minutes later and named a different file. The fix escapes the braces, which the accepted escape alphabet of v1.compiler.tokenize escape_decoding provides (open-brace and close-brace follow the backslash); that alphabet is why the naive fix -- escaping the delimiter instead -- is what tripped gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.authored_quotation_terminates_the_string_it_is_authored_in in the same cut.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
